The newly added props `onAmountChange` and `onNegativeChange` on `IOURequestStepConfirmationProps` have no `/** ... */` block comments, and no prop in the inline type block is documented. Per STYLE.md every component prop should carry a `/** */` block describing its purpose. The equivalent props were documented in `Provider.tsx`, `context.ts`, and `MoneyRequestConfirmationList.tsx`, so these should match for consistency.

Add a JSDoc block above each new prop:

```tsx
{
    shouldHideHeader?: boolean;

    /** Reports changes to the numeric digits of the inline amount field (new manual expense flow) */
    onAmountChange?: (digits: string) => void;

    /** Reports whether the inline amount is negative (new manual expense flow) */
    onNegativeChange?: (isNegative: boolean) => void;
}
```

The new `HomePageSkeletonCardProps` type declares props (`numRows`, `renderRow`, `shouldShowSeparators`) but none of them has a `/** ... */` block comment. Every component prop must be documented at its definition site.

Add a doc block above each prop:
```tsx
type HomePageSkeletonCardProps = {
    /** Number of skeleton rows to render inside the card */
    numRows: number;

    /** Renders a single skeleton row from the provided geometry */
    renderRow: (args: SkeletonRowArgs) => React.ReactNode;

    /** Whether to draw a bottom border between rows */
    shouldShowSeparators?: boolean;
};
```

`HeaderTitleSubtitleLinkProps` is a newly added props type whose only prop (`children`) has no `/** ... */` block comment. Per `STYLE.md`, component props must be documented at their definition site.

```tsx
type HeaderTitleSubtitleLinkProps = {
    /** The URL to open, also rendered as the link text */
    children: string;
};
```

`HeaderTitleSubtitleProps` is a newly added props type whose only prop (`children`) has no `/** ... */` block comment. Per `STYLE.md`, component props must be documented at their definition site.

