The newly added `OptionsWarmerProps` type declares the `onDone` prop with no `/** ... */` block comment. Per `STYLE.md`, every component prop should be documented with a JSDoc block comment so its purpose is clear at the definition site. Note the sibling `SearchRouterOptionsWarmerProps` type already documents the same prop.

Add a block comment above the prop:

```tsx
type OptionsWarmerProps = {
    /** Called once the option list is cached (or the warm is no longer needed), so the parent can unmount this component. */
    onDone: () => void;
};
```

The new `AutoGrowHeightInputContainerProps` type declares three props (`children`, `measureContent`, `style`) and none of them has a `/** ... */` block comment. Per STYLE.md every component prop must be documented at its definition site.

Add a JSDoc block above each prop:

```tsx
type AutoGrowHeightInputContainerProps = {
    /** Render prop that receives the measured max height available for the auto-growing input */
    children: (maxAutoGrowHeight: number) => ReactNode;

    /** Overrides how the inner content height is measured (defaults to measuring the content View) */
    measureContent?: (content: View | null, callback: (contentHeight: number) => void) => void;

    /** Style applied to the outer ScrollView container */
    style?: StyleProp<ViewStyle>;
};
```

This new `TitleProps` type declares its own props (`children`, `style`) but none of them has a `/** ... */` block comment. Per STYLE.md every component prop should be documented at its definition site.

Add a JSDoc block above each prop:

```tsx
type TitleProps = {
    /** Title content, rendered as a headline when a string */
    children?: ReactNode;

    /** Additional style applied to the title text */
