This new `DescriptionProps` type declares its own props (`children`, `shouldRenderHTML`) but none of them has a `/** ... */` block comment. Per STYLE.md every component prop should be documented at its definition site so its purpose is clear. `shouldRenderHTML` in particular is non-obvious and warrants a description.

Add a JSDoc block above each prop:

```tsx
type DescriptionProps = {
    /** Description text to render */
    children?: string;

    /** Whether the description text is HTML markup and should be rendered via RenderHTML */
    shouldRenderHTML?: boolean;
};
```

The new `SearchNLFilterContentProps` type declares three props (`onSuccess`, `containerStyle`, `buttonContainerStyle`) but none of them has a `/** ... */` block comment. Per STYLE.md every component prop must be documented at the definition site.

```tsx
type SearchNLFilterContentProps = {
    /** Called with the destination route once the query is successfully parsed */
    onSuccess: (route: Route) => void;

    /** Optional style override for the input container */
