The newly added `policyID` prop is the only own member declared on `UserSelectorProps`, and it has no `/** ... */` block comment above it. Per STYLE.md, every component prop should be documented with a block comment at its definition site so its purpose is clear — especially important here since the prop is typed as `Filter | undefined` (the selected workspace filter), not a plain policy ID, which is not obvious from the name.

Add a JSDoc block above the prop:

```tsx
type UserSelectorProps = SearchFilterCommonProps<string[] | undefined> & {
    /** The currently selected workspace filter, used to limit suggestions to those workspaces' members */
    policyID: Filter | undefined;
};
```

This newly added component props type declares its own prop but none of its members carry a `/** ... */` block comment. Per `STYLE.md`, every component prop should be documented with a JSDoc block comment at its definition site.

```tsx
type ConnectToDualEntryFlowProps = {
