The newly added `ExportDownloadStatusProviderProps` type declares the `children` prop with no `/** ... */` block comment. Per `STYLE.md`, every component prop should be documented with a JSDoc block comment so its purpose is clear at the definition site. Note the sibling `ExportDownloadStatusContextValue` type already documents `trackExport`.

Add a doc comment above the prop, or reuse the shared `ChildrenProps` type (`src/types/utils/ChildrenProps.ts`):

```tsx
type ExportDownloadStatusProviderProps = {
    /** The subtree that can trigger and observe the export status modal */
    children: React.ReactNode;
};
```

The new `EnableTravelSubPageProps` type declares three of its own new members (`policy`, `policyID`, `resolvedDomain`) on top of the intersected `SubPageProps`, but none of them carries a `/** ... */` block comment. Per `STYLE.md`, each prop a type introduces must be documented with a JSDoc block comment. (The intersection with the documented `SubPageProps` base is fine, but the members declared here still need their own docs.)

Add a `/** */` block above each newly declared prop, e.g.:

```tsx
type EnableTravelSubPageProps = SubPageProps & {
    /** The workspace being enabled for travel */
    policy: OnyxEntry<Policy>;

    /** ID of the workspace being enabled for travel */
    policyID: string;

    /** The provisioning domain resolved for this flow session */
    resolvedDomain: string;
};
```

The new `EnableTravelContentProps` type declares five of its own props (`policy`, `policyID`, `account`, `privatePersonalDetails`, `travelProvisioning`) but none of them carries a `/** ... */` block comment. Per `STYLE.md`, every component prop must be documented with a JSDoc block comment at the definition site so its purpose is clear.

Add a `/** */` block above each prop, e.g.:

```tsx
type EnableTravelContentProps = {
    /** The workspace being enabled for travel */
    policy: OnyxEntry<Policy>;

    /** ID of the workspace being enabled for travel */
    policyID: string;

    /** The current user's account, used to check validation status */
    account: OnyxEntry<Account>;

    /** The current user's private personal details, used to detect a missing legal name */
    privatePersonalDetails: OnyxEntry<PrivatePersonalDetails>;

    /** Persisted provisioning session state (frozen step list, selected domain, tax ID) */
    travelProvisioning: OnyxEntry<TravelProvisioning>;
};
```

