The `AgentsTableProps` type introduces three new props (`canSelectAgents`, `selectedKeys`, `onRowSelectionChange`) and none of the props in the type carry a `/** ... */` block comment describing their purpose. Per STYLE.md, every component prop should be documented at the definition site so its intent is clear.

Add a JSDoc block above each new prop, e.g.:

```tsx
type AgentsTableProps = {
    /** The list of agents to render as rows */
    agents: AgentRowData[];

    /** Whether rows can be selected (enables selection UI) */
    canSelectAgents: boolean;

    /** Keys of the currently selected rows */
    selectedKeys: string[];

    /** Called with the updated selected row keys when the selection changes */
    onRowSelectionChange: (selectedRowKeys: string[]) => void;
};
```
